pi-economics is MIT-licensed (LICENSE). It builds one upstream extension
from its source and applies the patches under patches/<input>/ to it.
The patches are derived from that project and are distributed under its
licence; the upstream's licence text, with its permission notice, is kept
next to its patches as patches/<input>/LICENSE.

The checks install their npm toolchain from a third party's manifest, kept
byte for byte: checks/npm/package.json and its lockfile are pi-retry's own
(https://github.com/monotykamary/pi-retry — MIT (package.json, README),
author Tom X Nguyen). pi-economics no longer builds or ships pi-retry.
Licence text: checks/npm/LICENSE (the upstream ships no LICENSE file; the
text is the standard MIT licence for its package.json declaration).

